    "temperament": "territorial",
    "refuge": "rift",
    "fears": "sunlight",
    "words": {
      "Warns": "A pressure comes into your head, not quite a voice. It is aware of you, and it is not afraid.",
      "Flinches": "The light of a summer noon comes into the cavern with you, and the pressure in your head becomes a sound like a held breath let go. The thing in the vein draws back from the light, slowly, the way a tide goes out, into the rift at the back of the cavern."
