    "item": "noonlight",
    "role": "strongroom",
    "seen": "On the top shelf, behind the balance, stands a jar of thick old glass stoppered with lead, and it is full of light: not lamplight, but daylight, the colour of noon.",
    "cut": "IT CANNOT BEAR THE NOON. THE PAYMASTER KEEPS NOON IN A JAR.",
    "fact": "What the Delvers walled in below their mine cannot bear the light of noon; their paymaster kept noon in a jar."
  },
