    "item": "the heart of the vein",
    "kind": "star_iron_heart",
    "text": "The Delvers went down after the star-iron until their last gallery broke into the heart of the vein, and what lived in it. Whoever brings up the heart has what the Delvers died for.",
    "goal": "Bring the heart of the vein up out of {name}, from below the Delvers' last gallery.",
    "raised": "In the daylight the heart of the vein, up out of {name} at last, is heavier than it was in the dark, and it has stopped humming."
  },
  "rumours": [
    "'The Delvers' mine at {name}? There is still ore down there, they say, the pale kind. Nobody goes below the first level. The cage hangs in the shaft and the wheel will not turn.'",
    "'My grandfather went into {name} after the star-iron. He said the stair at the bottom was walled up by the Delvers themselves, and there was writing on it, and he came back up without reading it.'"
  ],
  "land": {
    "blight": "The heather stops a long stride short of the adit mouth all round, as though it had been burned back, and grows again beyond. Nothing nests in the spoil.",
    "signs": {
      "woodcraft": "There is no track into the adit that is not a man's, and the foxes' runs bend wide of it. Only at noon, with the sun full on the hillside, do the ravens come down and sit on the spoil.",
      "digging": "The last of the spoil, at the top of the heap, is not the same stone as the rest: black, glassy, as if it had been in a fire. The Delvers' last gallery broke into something that was not rock."
    },
    "healed": "The heather has begun to creep back toward the adit mouth, and a wheatear has a nest in the spoil."
  },
  "camp": {
    "scene": "Someone camped here, and not so long ago: a ring of stones round dead ashes, a bedroll gone stiff with damp, a pack with its straps cut. They did not come back for any of it.",
    "journal": [
      "A damp notebook, the last pages written small to save them. 'The cage is at the bottom and the wheel will not turn: rusted. Brann says a bar under the axle would free it, if we had brought one. The ladders in the winze are sound as far as we went. Something lives in the props by the adit; it bit Edda.'",
      "A damp notebook, the last pages written small. 'The stair at the end of the haulage is walled up, and there is writing on it nobody can read. Under the pump-room the shaft is full of water. Edda says the wheel was turned by water from above, and that is what the dry channel up by the spring is for. She wants to try it. I want to go home.'",
      "A damp notebook, the last page hardly legible. 'Past the furnace the cut goes down, and the cold comes up it like breath. Brann went down with a rope. The rope came up.'",
      "A notebook with one line in it, written by someone lying down: 'it is not asleep'."
