data/goings-on/disputation/situation.kyr:
Module disputation "The disputation on the green" {
  Description "On market days two philosophers dispute on the green, and the town stands round to listen and take sides: one of the One, who teaches that all things are one thing and change is only seeming, and one of the Flow, who teaches that nothing stays. A sophist leans between them, and will argue either side for whoever pays. What the country's own history says would settle it, for whoever has found it.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  // The country's own history, for whoever has found it: who the first makers were, by their own marks, which still
  // read after them; how they ended; and the kingdom after them, and how it fell.
  Entity making: fact "Who the first makers were". Entity ending: fact "How the first makers ended".
  Entity successors: fact "The kingdom after them".
  Entity oneness: claim "that all things are one, and change is only seeming".
  Entity flux: claim "that nothing stays, and nothing made outlasts its making".
  Initially Assert refutes(making, flux). Initially Assert refutes(ending, oneness). Initially Assert refutes(successors, oneness).
  Entity dispute: fact "Two philosophers dispute on {green} on market days, one of the One and one of the Flow, and the town takes sides.".
  Initially Assert established(dispute).

  Person one "The philosopher of the One" at green { Role "a philosopher of the One". Peaceable. }
  Person flow "The philosopher of the Flow" at green { Role "a philosopher of the Flow". Peaceable. }
  Person sophist "The sophist" at green { Role "a sophist". Peaceable. }
  Initially Assert believes(one, oneness). Initially Set conviction(one, oneness) to 3. Initially Assert disputant(one).
  Initially Assert believes(flow, flux). Initially Set conviction(flow, flux) to 3. Initially Assert disputant(flow).
  Initially Set hire(one) to 0. Initially Set hire(flow) to 0.
  Relation heard(group). Relation answered(group, entity). Relation glanced(group).
  Entity move_reason: fact "a reason". Entity move_after: fact "the kingdom after". Entity move_argue: fact "an argument".
  Entity move_sophist: fact "the sophist". Entity move_glance: fact "the old stones".

  Observe crowd at green when believes(one, oneness) and believes(flow, flux) "Two philosophers are disputing on {green}, and a crowd stands round them: {one}, who holds that all things are one and change is only seeming, and {flow}, who holds that nothing stays. {sophist} leans between them with folded arms, and laughs at both.".
  Observe one_beaten at green when doubts(one, oneness) and not reasoned(one, oneness) "The crowd has gone over from {one} today, and laughs when {one} tries to speak.".
  Observe flow_beaten at green when doubts(flow, flux) and not reasoned(flow, flux) "The crowd has gone over from {flow} today, and laughs when {flow} tries to speak.".
  Observe one_recanted at green when reasoned(one, oneness) "{one} no longer teaches the One: things end, {one} tells whoever will listen, and the end of them is not seeming.".
  Observe flow_recanted at green when reasoned(flow, flux) "{flow} no longer teaches the Flow: some things stay, {flow} tells whoever will listen, longer than the hands that made them.".
  Observe one_cold near one when scorns(one, party) "{one} turns away from you.".
  Observe flow_cold near flow when scorns(flow, party) "{flow} turns away from you.".
  // Someone in the company who reads people sees it without being asked (a passive check: no roll): the philosopher
  // of the Flow keeps looking at the oldest stones in the town while saying that nothing stays.
  Entity glance: fact "The philosopher of the Flow looks at the oldest stones in the town every time the Flow is taught.".
  Initially Assert refutes(glance, flux).
  Observe flow_looks at green as sign when capable(party, insight) and believes(flow, flux) and not knows(party, glance) "Watching {flow} argue, you see where {flow}'s eyes go at each 'nothing stays': to the oldest stones in the town, which were old when the town was new." teaches glance.

  Topic one_doctrine with one "Ask {one} what the One is" when true once {
    Says "'There is one thing,' says {one}, 'and it does not change. The river, the hill, you and I and the dead: one thing, seen in pieces by eyes that see in pieces. What seems to end does not end. Nothing is lost, because nothing is apart.' The crowd murmurs; some of them nod.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(one). }
  }
  Topic flow_doctrine with flow "Ask {flow} what the Flow is" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing stays,' says {flow}. 'Not the river, not the hill, not the stones you stand on. What is made is unmade in the making; your house is already falling down. Hold on to nothing, and nothing will be taken from you.' The other half of the crowd laughs and claps.".
    On discuss { Assert heard(flow). }
  }
  Topic sophist_holds with sophist "Ask {sophist} what a sophist holds" when true once {
    Says "'Nothing at all,' says {sophist}, cheerfully. 'The truth is whatever is left standing when the arguing stops, and I can see to it that it is yours. Two coin, and I will argue either of them into the ground.'".
  }

  // Against the Flow: the makers' own marks, which still read though the makers are long gone.
  Action answer_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Answer {flow} with the makers' own marks, which still read though they are gone" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_reason) and knows(actor, making).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_reason). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 3. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). Assert willing(flow, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {flow} what the first makers cut in their stones, and that it still reads, when no one alive has seen a maker. {flow} is quiet a long time. 'Then some things stay,' {flow} says at last, loud enough for the green to hear, 'longer than the hands that made them. I have taught wrong.' Afterwards {flow} comes to you: 'If you are going where the old words are, I would read them with you.'".
    Otherwise "You tell {flow} of the makers' marks, but you tell it badly, and {flow} turns it into a joke about stones that the crowd likes better.".
  }
  Action answer_flow_glance(actor: group, site: place) "Ask {flow} why the old stones draw the eye of one who says that nothing stays" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_glance) and knows(actor, glance).
    Resolve check(actor, insight, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_glance). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 3. Assert reasoned(flow, flux). Assert willing(flow, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_glance). }
    Result "{flow} looks at the shrine's stones, and then at you. 'Because they are still there,' {flow} says. 'I have looked at them every market day for twenty years, and said that nothing stays.' {flow} laughs. 'Some things stay. I will say so.' And to you, quietly: 'If you go anywhere old, take me.'".
    Otherwise "{flow} only smiles. 'I look at them,' {flow} says, 'to see them going.' The crowd likes it.".
  }
  // Against the One: how the first makers ended, and the kingdom after them, which also ended.
  Action answer_one(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} how the first makers ended" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_reason) and knows(actor, ending).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_easy).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_reason). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 3. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). Assert willing(one, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_reason). }
    Result "You tell {one} how the first makers ended, as their own stones tell it. {one} listens to the end, and the crowd with {one}. 'A people,' {one} says, 'and then not. That is not seeming.' {one} sits down heavily. 'I will have to think again from the beginning.' Then, to you: 'You know where the old things are. Let me come with you, and see them end for myself.'".
    Otherwise "You tell {one} how the makers ended, but {one} hears it out and smiles: 'They are here still, in the One, as you are.' The crowd nods along.".
  }
  Action answer_one_after(actor: group, site: place) "Tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, and how it fell" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_after) and knows(actor, successors).
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_after). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 3. Assert reasoned(one, oneness). Assert willing(one, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_after). }
    Result "You tell {one} of the kingdom that came after the makers, what it was and how it fell, with the names in it. 'Twice, then,' {one} says. 'Twice in this one country, a whole people ended.' {one} looks round at the town as if seeing it for the first time. 'I was wrong. Let me come with you, and see what else ends.'".
    Otherwise "{one} lets you finish. 'Kingdoms are seeming,' {one} says, 'like the clouds,' and the crowd is with {one} again.".
  }
  // Argument without a reason: it wins the day and is gone by morning, and is not forgiven.
  Action argue_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {flow} down: some things stay" {
    Speaker flow. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow) and believes(flow, flux)
      and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_argue).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 3. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(flow, move_argue). }
    Result "You turn {flow}'s own words on {flow}, faster than {flow} can answer, until the crowd is laughing and {flow} has nothing to say. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{flow} lets you talk yourself out, and then says one thing, and the crowd laughs at you instead.".
  }
  Action argue_one(actor: group, site: place) "Argue {one} down: things change" {
    Speaker one. Time 5 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one) and believes(one, oneness)
      and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_argue).
    Resolve check(actor, persuasion, dc_hard).
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_argue). Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 3. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    On failure { Assert answered(one, move_argue). }
    Result "You tie {one} in {one}'s own knots, one after another, until the crowd is jeering and {one} stops trying to answer. It is a victory. It is not a reason.".
    Otherwise "{one} answers every point with the same calm, and the crowd tires of you first.".
  }
  // The sophist argues for whoever pays: the day is won, and nothing else.
  Action hire_sophist_flow(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {flow} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(flow, site) and heard(flow)
      and believes(flow, flux) and not scorns(flow, actor) and not answered(flow, move_sophist) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(flow, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(flow, flux) by 3. Assert swayedBy(flow, flux, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {flow}, and takes {flow} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }
  Action hire_sophist_one(actor: group, site: place) "Pay {sophist} two coin to argue {one} into the ground" {
    Speaker sophist. Time 10 minutes.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(sophist, site) and at(one, site) and heard(one)
      and believes(one, oneness) and not scorns(one, actor) and not answered(one, move_sophist) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 2.
    On success { Assert answered(one, move_sophist). Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 2. Increase quantity(sophist, gold) by 2.
      Decrease conviction(one, oneness) by 3. Assert swayedBy(one, oneness, actor). }
    Result "{sophist} pockets the coin, steps up beside {one}, and takes {one} apart in a quarter of an hour, cheerfully, to the delight of the green. Then {sophist} winks at you. 'By tomorrow,' {sophist} says, 'it will all be believed again. It always is.'".
  }

  Objective disputed when knows(party, dispute) and believes(one, oneness) and believes(flow, flux) "Two philosophers dispute on {green}: the One against the Flow. What the country's own history says could settle it.".
  Goal reasoned(one, oneness) or reasoned(flow, flux).
}

data/goings-on/drover/situation.kyr:
Module drover "The drover who did not come home" {
  Description "A drover went out on the road three days ago with a cart and two oxen and did not come home. His dog did, alone, in the night. His wife cooks at the inn and will not talk about it; his son talks of nothing else.".
  Entity party: group "Your company".
  Place green "The green" is room.
  Place taproom "The taproom" is room.
  Place road "The road" is room.
  Relation told(group). Relation gone(group).
  Entity missing: fact "A drover went out on the road from {green} three days ago and did not come home. His dog did.".
  Initially Assert established(missing). Initially Assert staged(road, missing).

  Person wife "The drover's wife" at taproom { Role "the drover's wife, who cooks at the inn". Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  Person son "The drover's son" at green { Role "the drover's son, who wants to go after his father". Pronouns he. Peaceable. }
  // The dog that came home: a real dog, lame in the off forefoot, who lets anyone who is kind to her look at her; and
  // whoever does sees where she has been.
  Person dog "the grey dog" at green { Role "the drover's dog". Species dog. Pronouns she. Peaceable. }
  Observe dog_waits near dog of dog when not told(wife) and at(dog, green) "A grey dog lies by the door of {taproom} with her head on her paws, watching the road. She holds one forefoot off the ground.".
  Observe dog_in near dog of dog when told(wife) and at(dog, taproom) "The grey dog lies by the kitchen fire with her chin on her paws.".
  Rule dog_goes_in when told(wife) and at(dog, green) { Assert at(dog, taproom). }
  Entity dog_mud: fact "The grey dog came home caked in black ditch-mud, the off forefoot cut as if on iron.".
  Observe dog_tells near dog as sign when petted(dog, party) and not knows(party, dog_mud) "Under your hand her coat is stiff with dried black mud to the belly: ditch-mud, not road dust, as if she had lain a long time somewhere low and wet. The pad of the off forefoot is cut clean across, the way iron cuts." teaches dog_mud.
  Observe dog_muddy near dog of dog as sign when knows(party, dog_mud) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Her coat is stiff with black ditch-mud to the belly.".
  Observe ruts at road when not knows(party, found_cart) "Fresh ruts run off the edge of the road here, where the bank drops away.".

  Discovery found_cart "The drover's cart went off the road in the night. He is under it, a day or more dead, and whatever had the oxen dragged them off toward the hills." {
    Found by searching road "Below the road, where the bank drops away, a cart lies on its side in the ditch with a man under it, a day or more dead. The oxen are gone; something had them, and dragged them off toward the hills. His knife is still in his belt.".
  }
  Item knife "a drover's knife with a horn handle" is dagger at road hidden until found_cart.

  // To one of the family the drover is a father, his wife a mother, his son a brother: they say other things.
  Observe wife_kin near wife when kin(party, wife) and not told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth with her back to the room.".
  Observe son_kin near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, green) "Your brother is sitting on a rail with your father's old spear across his knees, watching the road. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  Observe son_kin_in near son when kin(party, son) and not told(son) and at(son, taproom) "Your brother sits by the kitchen fire with your father's old spear across his knees, not drinking. He is taller by a head than when you went away.".
  // Until he has somewhere to go, the son keeps the green by day and comes in to his mother after dark.
  Rule son_goes_in when dark() and at(son, green) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, taproom). }
  Rule son_comes_out when not dark() and at(son, taproom) and not willing(son, party) { Assert at(son, green). }
  Observe son_kin_ready near son when kin(party, son) and told(son) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Your brother is waiting by the rail with the spear, ready when you are.".
  Observe wife_kin_told near wife when kin(party, wife) and told(wife) "Your mother is at the hearth. She looks up when you come in, and goes back to her work.".
  Topic wife_where with wife "Ask your mother where he was going" when kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "'Out on {road}, with the salt for the reed-cutters,' says {wife}, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'Three days there and back, the way he goes. The dog came home on the fourth, lame in the off foot.' She wipes her hands, though they are dry. 'Nobody will go and look. I am glad you came.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told_kin with wife "Tell your mother what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, wife) and not told(wife) once {
    Says "{wife} does not sit down. She takes your face in her hands and looks at it for a long time. 'I knew,' she says. 'The dog knew.' Then she goes back to the pot, because there are people to feed.".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). }
  }
  Topic son_plan with son "Ask {son} what he means to do" when kin(actor, son) and not knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(son) once {
    Says "'Go after him,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited three days.' He looks at you, and at the road. 'If you are going, I am coming with you. If you are not, I am going anyway.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  Topic son_found_kin with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and kin(actor, son) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out, and is quiet for a long time. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  Topic wife_husband with wife "Ask {wife} about her husband" when not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "'He went out with the cart three days back,' says {wife}, and keeps her eyes on the pot. 'The dog came home. He didn't.'".
  }
  Topic wife_told with wife "Tell {wife} what you found on the road" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(actor, wife) once {
    Says "{wife} puts down the ladle and sits. After a while she says, 'I knew. The dog knew.' She takes coin from her apron and puts it in your hand without counting it. 'For going.'".
    On discuss { Assert told(wife). Increase quantity(actor, gold) by 6. }
  }
  Topic wife_knife with wife "Show {wife} her husband's knife" when carries(actor, knife) and told(wife) once {
    Says "She turns the knife over in her hands, and gives it back. 'Keep it. He would want it used, not hung on a wall.'".
  }
  Topic son_father with son "Ask {son} about his father" when not knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son) once {
    Says "'Three days,' says {son}. 'Mother says wait. I have waited.' He looks at the road. 'If you are going that way, I will come.'".
  }
  Topic son_found with son "Tell {son} what you found" when knows(actor, found_cart) and not kin(actor, son) once {
    Says "{son} hears it out. 'Then whatever had the oxen is still out there,' he says. 'I am coming with you. No hire. I want to see it.'".
    On discuss { Assert willing(son, actor). Assert told(son). }
  }
  // Once he has come with you, the son talks on the way: he knows the road his father took, and the cart.
  Topic son_road with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road your father took" when kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'{road}, to market. He knew every rut of it.' {son} kicks at a stone. 'He had the left wheel out of true all spring and would not see to it. If the cart went off the road, look for where a wheel like that would take it.'".
  }
  Topic son_road_stranger with son travelling "Ask {son} about the road his father took" when not kin(actor, son) and awake(member_son_person) and not knows(actor, found_cart) once {
    Says "'{road}, to market,' says {son}. 'He knew it in the dark. The left wheel of the cart was out of true. If it went off the road, that is why.'".
  }
  Topic son_night with son travelling "Sit up late with {son}" when awake(member_son_person) and dark() once {
    Says "'He used to sing to the oxen,' says {son}. 'Terrible songs. He made them up as he went, and they liked them better than anything.' He is quiet a while. 'Mother would not have him sing in the house.'".
  }
  Event son_wheel at road when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and at(party, road) and not knows(party, found_cart) "{son} stops where the ruts go off the road and stands looking at them. 'That is the left wheel,' he says. 'That is his.'".
  Entity son_knelt: fact "Your brother knelt by the cart.".
  Observe son_kneels at road as event when travelsWith(son, party) and awake(member_son_person) and knows(party, found_cart) and not knows(party, son_knelt) "{son} goes down the bank to the cart before anyone can stop him, and kneels there a long time. When he comes back up he has nothing to say, and nobody asks him to." teaches son_knelt.
  // Left alone too long, the son goes out after his father himself.
  Rule son_goes when watch(clock) >= 204 and not told(son) and at(son, green) says "{son} has taken his father's old spear and gone out on the road alone. Nobody stopped him." { Retract at(son, green). Assert gone(son). }

  Objective road when knows(party, missing) and not knows(party, found_cart) and not kin(party, wife) "A drover from {green} went out on the road and did not come home.".
  Objective tell when knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) and not kin(party, wife) "The drover's wife, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  Objective road_kin when kin(party, wife) and not knows(party, found_cart) "Your father went out on {road} with the cart, and did not come home.".
  Objective tell_kin when kin(party, wife) and knows(party, found_cart) and not told(wife) "Your mother, at the inn, does not know what you found.".
  Goal told(wife).
}

